# You do NOT need this file on your own computer: `npm start` works without it.
# Online (Netlify), these same names go in Netlify → Site configuration → Environment variables.
# The README's "Put it online" section explains each one.

# Supabase → Connect → "Transaction pooler" connection string, with your database password filled in
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.abcdefghijklmnopqrst:YOUR-PASSWORD@aws-0-ap-south-1.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres

# Any long random text (run `npm run secret` to make one). Encrypts your saved Meta details.
# Keep it safe and never change it, or you will need to enter your Meta details again.
# SECRET_KEY=

# Supabase → Project Settings → API Keys → anon / publishable key (for instant updates between devices)
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Advanced, only on your own computer:
# PORT=3000
# DATA_DIR=./data
